==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Lumbercat''' at level 10

Evolves into '''Weedwacker Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Gardener Cat works in a similar way to [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]], attacking incredibly fast to make up for a low chance to trigger his ability.

Send him out to support your attackers and meatshields against zombies, as Gardener can stop them from wrecking havoc in the middle of your army when they revive or unburrow, as well as simply lowering the pressure on the frontline by paralyzing a single zombie. He can also help a lot in [[Unholy Tempest (Insane)|The Rolling Dead]] due to [[Zyclone]]'s low range and speed, making it easy to create a stack. On top of all of that he has Zombie Killer, giving you a higher chance at getting rid of the Zyclone for good.

His attack speed make him decently fast at dispatching [[Metal Doge]]s, [[Metal Hippoe]]s or [[Croconator]]s, assuming the magnification isn't high. While he's not recommended to bring exclusively for that purpose, it may still be worth considering in rare scenarios when the stage also features Zombies.

==='''True Form'''===
The increased freeze duration is a huge help for this cat, as it gives more time until the next freeze, effectively making it easier to permafreeze zombies. The increased range and health help a lot as well with his survivability, also making him easier to stack. It's a pretty noticeable upgrade, definitely worth the catfruit if you wish to use this unit.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Target Aku''' is undoubtedly useful, as it basically doubles Weedwacker's scope by adding a new trait to target; unfortunately, the Aku are about the worst possible match-up for this cat. Some have Shields that block status effects, it gets outranged by a lot of them, and death surges can easily kill it. '''Resist Surge''' and '''HP Buff''' both help a little, both against Aku and in general, but it would take a lot of +levels too for this support-type cat to reliably live long enough to have an effect in endgame scenarios. '''Attack Buff''' on a Zombie Killer is always good, as it's essentially a small extra chance to have a potentially strong Zombie not revive, not destroy the cat army from the middle and not withhold its bounty for longer. '''Resist Slow''' is situational, consider unlocking it if a situation requires it.

==='''Orb'''===
If the Target Aku and Resist Surge talents are unlocked and fully upgraded, then a Resist Surge orb can give Weedwacker full Surge immunity. Do note that it requires both an S-Rank orb and a Level 10 Resist Surge Talent.

Due to the low Aku compatibility otherwise, attack or defense orbs for Zombies are recommended. If you go all out on +levels and defensive talents, defense up for Aku is good too.

Cash Back is useful for cheaper spamming. Death Mini-Surge is actually a rather poor choice for Weedwacker due to only having a 5% chance to freeze.

